{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788269180,"nonce":"uwphjFfpXAgSfu0MydrPob8LFH0=","message":"ALREADY SHIPPED — closing on evidence, not on work. Verified 2026-09-01 by the round that follows session 13, during its verify-first pass.\n\nThe fix landed in `28d52ae` (\"map-view: publish the alphabet identity map-dump already names\") and the issue was never closed. A session planning this round listed it as outstanding work; it is not.\n\nWHAT IS IN THE CODE\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/Spatial.cs`, class `CropRenderer`:\n\n    public const string AlphabetId = \"map-view/ascii-1\";\n\nemitted by `Render` in a `channel` block:\n\n    [\"channel\"] = { [\"name\"] = \"map-view\",\n                    [\"alphabet\"] = AlphabetId,\n                    [\"distinct_from\"] = \"baseviz-catalog/1\",\n                    [\"note\"] = ... }\n\n`MapDumpVerbs.cs` publishes the mirror image in the same field and the same\nshape: `name` \"map-dump\", `alphabet` \"baseviz-catalog/1\", `distinct_from`\n\"map-view/ascii-1\". Symmetric, and each names the other.\n\nBULLET BY BULLET\n\n1. \"`map-view` publishes an alphabet identity in the same field and format\n   `map-dump` does.\" SATISFIED, literally — same `channel.alphabet` key, same\n   string format.\n\n2. \"Two renders of the same rect through the two channels can be shown to share\n   an alphabet by comparing that field alone.\" RESOLVED DIFFERENTLY, and better\n   than asked. The two channels do NOT share an alphabet and never should: one\n   is a single ASCII char per cell over a collapsed priority, the other is\n   2-char def-catalog tokens per layer with colour. The bullet presumed a shared\n   table. What shipped instead is that each channel names the other in\n   `distinct_from`, so a consumer comparing them cell-for-cell can detect the\n   mistake by field rather than discovering it as a mysterious disagreement.\n   That is the property the issue actually wanted — \"when the two disagree there\n   is no way to tell a real divergence from two different alphabets\" — reached by\n   declaring the difference rather than by erasing it.\n\n3. \"A change to the symbol table changes the identity, so a stale consumer can\n   detect it.\" SATISFIED BY CONVENTION, NOT BY MECHANISM, and that is the one\n   residual. The code comment states the rule precisely — bump the trailing\n   number, and `map-dump`'s `distinct_from` with it, on any change to the reserved\n   band, the layer priority in `Cell()`, or the def-to-char derivation; adding a\n   legend ENTRY is not a change to the table. Nothing enforces it.\n\nTHE RESIDUAL, OWNED RATHER THAN LEFT\n\nNo acceptance suite asserts `map-view` publishes `channel.alphabet` at all —\n`grep alphabet accept/` hits one prose line in `2.5-png-render.md` and no check.\nSo a regression that dropped the field would go unnoticed, which is the same\nshape as the traps `accept/`'s own convention exists to catch (\"assert the key\nexists, never eq(None)\"). Handed to the geometry cluster of the current round as\na one-line shape check rather than left as a note here.","files":null}]}